# The app image's build context.
#
# A root .dockerignore also applies to any other image built from this
# directory unless that image has its own <dockerfile>.dockerignore. The MCP
# image is built from here too (`docker build -f mcp/Dockerfile .`) and now has
# one, but `mcp` is deliberately NOT excluded here as well: the per-Dockerfile
# file is a BuildKit feature, and if a build ever runs without BuildKit the
# fallback is this file. Excluding mcp/ here would then empty the MCP image's
# context again, and the failure reads "/mcp/src: not found" in a job that
# looks unrelated - which is exactly how it went the first time.
#
# The cost is a few hundred kilobytes of extra context for the app image, which
# copies its sources explicitly and ignores the rest.
node_modules
dist
src-tauri
.git
.github
docs
packaging
backend
frontend
k8s
tests
*.md
# ...except the wallpaper credits, which are served by the app rather than
# being repository documentation. `*.md` had quietly dropped them, so the
# container answered 404 for /wallpapers/CREDITS.md while happily serving the
# seven photographs it names.
!public/wallpapers/CREDITS.md
